---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Fuel and Wellness App';
const description = 'Evidence-based nutrition and wellness guidance for training, recovery, sleep, stress and overall wellbeing.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
<section class="page-hero orange-bg"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow orange-text">Fuel & Wellness</div><h1>Nutrition and lifestyle guidance that supports performance.</h1><p class="lead">Fuel & Wellness connects training with practical nutrition, protein education, sleep, stress, hydration and recovery habits.</p></div></section>
<section class="content"><div class="container"><article>
<h2>Why fuel and wellness belong with training</h2><p>Workouts are only one part of performance. The body also needs food, hydration, sleep, recovery time, and stress management. Fuel & Wellness helps users understand the lifestyle habits that make training more effective and sustainable.</p>
<p>This pillar is intentionally practical. Instead of focusing on extreme diets or confusing rules, it can teach simple habits like eating enough protein, building balanced meals, hydrating consistently, and supporting recovery with sleep.</p>
<div class="callout orange-border">Better fuel supports better training, better recovery, and better long-term health.</div>
<h2>Core Fuel & Wellness topics</h2>
<h3>Protein and recovery</h3><p>Protein supports muscle repair and helps users recover from training. A simple education module can explain why protein matters, how to spread it through the day, and how to think about it without overcomplicating meals.</p>
<h3>Hydration and energy</h3><p>Hydration affects energy, focus, performance, and recovery. Users do not need a complicated protocol to benefit from drinking enough fluids and paying attention to sweat, heat, and training intensity.</p>
<h3>Sleep and stress</h3><p>Sleep and stress affect how well people adapt to training. Fuel & Wellness can help users connect daily lifestyle choices with how they feel in workouts, recovery, mood, and motivation.</p>
<h2>Related guides</h2><div class="grid two"><a class="card" href="/nutrition/why-nutrition-is-important-for-athletes/"><h3>Why Nutrition Is Important for Athletes</h3><p>How food, hydration and recovery habits support performance.</p></a><a class="card" href="/fitness-apps/best-fitness-apps-with-nutrition/"><h3>Best Fitness Apps with Nutrition</h3><p>What to look for when choosing a fitness app with nutrition support.</p></a><a class="card" href="/fitness-apps/all-in-one-physical-mental-health-app/"><h3>All-in-One Wellness App Guide</h3><p>How fuel fits into training, recovery and mindset.</p></a><a class="card" href="/corporate-wellness/"><h3>Corporate Wellness Programs</h3><p>Why nutrition education belongs in workplace wellness.</p></a></div>
</article></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
